678
01:04:21,082 --> 01:04:32,145
[SPEAKER_01]: Ignorance really goes, and that you cannot rely on any of the preconceived notions that you have, and you have to be willing to put everything, throw everything out.

679
01:04:32,405 --> 01:04:36,806
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's again why there cannot be yoniso manasikāra without faith.

680
01:04:36,906 --> 01:04:40,207
[SPEAKER_01]: That is to say, you will not be able to go back far enough.

681
01:04:41,167 --> 01:04:53,617
[SPEAKER_01]: If you're not willing to question everything, even what you think the Buddha said and what you think the Buddha meant, because, see, even that, you do not have access to what the Buddha actually meant.

682
01:04:53,877 --> 01:04:55,759
[SPEAKER_01]: All you have is what you think the Buddha meant.

683
01:04:57,783 --> 01:05:04,824
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you always need to bear that in mind.

684
01:05:05,665 --> 01:05:07,685
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, that would prevent any kind of complacency.

685
01:05:08,345 --> 01:05:14,386
[SPEAKER_01]: And you would see then that... you would stop chasing after some specific insight.

686
01:05:15,086 --> 01:05:25,048
[SPEAKER_01]: You would just see, like, it's about... just wearing away that...

687
01:05:26,991 --> 01:05:28,393
[SPEAKER_01]: Wearing away those tendencies.

688
01:05:28,613 --> 01:05:31,876
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, eh... there's nothing to expect.

689
01:05:32,617 --> 01:05:34,639
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, am I wearing away the tendencies or not?

690
01:05:34,859 --> 01:05:35,520
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the question.

691
01:05:36,221 --> 01:05:37,762
[SPEAKER_01]: Not like what will happen at the end of it.

692
01:05:37,883 --> 01:05:40,425
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, what will happen at the end of it is the tendencies will wear away.

693
01:05:40,585 --> 01:05:40,926
[SPEAKER_01]: That's it.

